  "body": "Stacked on #1667 (the G30 logic of the Tormach lathe post). The diff shows the commits of #1667 until #1667 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `Dump` in `camcraft-post` gets the field `stock_turn_radius`. When it is set, finite and more than 0, the stream gets `PARAM StockTurnRadius` after `StockZTop`.\n- The new module `crates/app/src/stock_turn.rs` calculates the radius: the largest distance of a stock mesh vertex from the spindle axis (the world Z line through the setup origin).\n- `posting.rs` sets the radius only for a lathe or mill-turn setup. Mill streams do not change.\n- `tormach-lathe.cps`: `stockEnv()` uses the larger of the box half-width and `StockTurnRadius`. Thus the G30 approach and departure clear the rotating corners of a square bar.\n- `fanuc-lathe.cps` does not read the stock. It does not change.\n- `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` gets a row for the new property.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/1666-stock-turn-radius.md`.\n\n## Posted G-code changes\n\nYes, for a lathe program on a box (square bar) stock with the Tormach lathe post. The G30 departure goes to the corner diameter, not to the box width. A round bar gives the same radius as before, so its output does not change. No real control ran the output.\n\n## Updated goldens\n\nThe two axial-drill goldens now contain the corner-clearance departure:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach-lathe/axial_drill_mm.nc`: the last move changes from `G0 X24` to `G0 X33.941`.\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach-lathe/axial_drill_inch.nc`: the last move changes from `G0 X0.9449` to `G0 X1.3363`.\n\nThe fixture uses a 24 x 24 box stock. Its corners turn on a circle of radius 16.971 mm (diameter 33.941 mm). The updated goldens match this clearance. `lathe_post_tormach::an_axial_drill_posts_as_plain_moves_in_mm_and_inch` passes.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/lathe_post_turn_radius.rs`:\n\n- `a_lathe_stream_states_the_radius_its_stock_sweeps`\n- `a_mill_stream_states_no_turning_radius`\n- `the_g30_moves_use_the_square_bars_corner_circle`\n- `a_square_bar_program_has_no_g30_rapid_inside_the_corners_circle`\n\nAll four pass. The author-side validation on head `156dec8d689f539bfdcc01b3b39727af8d85dd02` reported a passing `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 421 post tests and 3023 app tests passed, with 22 app tests ignored. It also reported passing `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`.\n\nThe latest review tested a local trial merge with upstream main `4e0b9abefcb225595d47d9c69a2482d6359b190f`. All 96 selected app and post tests passed. These included all eight `lathe_post_tormach` tests and all four `lathe_post_turn_radius` tests. The review also reported passing `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`. It ran the quick-gate plan with `--dry-run`, rather than the full gate.\n\nThe author-side fix and the latest review checked mutations of the stream parameter and `stockEnv()` radius use. The tests failed with each mutation and passed after restoration. The author-side fix also checked the G30 motion-block test and each axial-drill golden by reverting each fix. Each test failed after the revert and passed after restoration.\n\nNot exercised: a real PathPilot control, mill-turn posts, and the UI.\n\nChangelog: The Tormach lathe post now clears the corners of a square-bar stock in its G30 approach and departure moves (the stream states StockTurnRadius).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nFixes #1666\n",
